      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "With the use of thermodilution techniques, changes in coronary sinus blood flow were measured during balloon catheter dilation of a high-grade stenosis within the left anterior descending coronary artery. Postdilation increases in flow occurred in a patient who experienced complete relief from previously incapacitating angina pectoris."},
